alse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs","anchor":"Required-reason-APIs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"